SUMMARY:Indios Amigos Traveling Exhibit at Gulf Breeze and Pace Libraries
DESCRIPTION:Gulf Breeze Library and then Pace Library host a bilingual tra
 veling exhibit from the Florida Public Archaeology Network for Hispanic H
 eritage Month. It tells the story of the Aztec artisans and warriors who 
 sailed with Tristan de Luna's 1559 expedition to Pensacola. The display s
 tays up all week at each branch\, so it fits a quick stop on a library vi
 sit.\nPrice: not published by the venue\, so confirm before you go\nArea:
